{"name":"Douro","hex":"#555500","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Douro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in northern Spain and Portugal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Douro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Douro","blocks":[{"text":"The Douro is the largest river of the Iberian Peninsula by discharge. It rises at the Pico de Urbión, the highest summit of the Picos de Urbión, first flows through Duruelo de la Sierra in the Spanish province of Soria, meanders briefly south, then flows generally west through the northern part of the Meseta Central in Castile and León into northern Portugal. Its largest tributary is the right-bank Esla. The Douro flows into the Atlantic Ocean at Porto, the second largest city of Portugal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Rio_Douro_-_Portugal_%2832615481975%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Rio_Douro_-_Portugal_%2832615481975%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douro"},{"title":"Douro (intermunicipal community)","blocks":[{"text":"The Comunidade Intermunicipal do Douro is an administrative division in Portugal. It replaced the Comunidade Urbana do Douro, created in 2004. It takes its name from the Douro River. The seat of the intermunicipal community is Vila Real. Douro comprises parts of the former districts of Bragança, Guarda, Vila Real and Viseu. The population in 2011 was 205,157, in an area of 4,031.58 square kilometres (1,556.60 mi2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Douro_region_logo.svg/330px-Douro_region_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douro_(intermunicipal_community)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Douro_%28fleuve%29.png/500px-Douro_%28fleuve%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut